{
  "_comment": [
    "Host settings fragment for the careful guardrail. Merge into your host's settings file",
    "(Claude Code: .claude/settings.json) — do not replace it wholesale.",
    "",
    "BOTH matchers are required and they do different jobs:",
    "  Bash                            — the destructive-command matcher.",
    "  Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit — refuses edits to the guard files themselves.",
    "Registering only the first leaves the guard deletable by one edit that nothing watches,",
    "which is how it stays inert while looking installed.",
    "",
    "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is a Claude Code variable. On another host, substitute an absolute",
    "path, and find that host's own PreToolUse decision contract before trusting the hook —",
    "the wrong JSON envelope is silently ignored, which is exactly how this guard shipped",
    "inert for 2.5 months. See skills/careful/SKILL.md.",
    "",
    "Verify with the two live probes in skills/careful/SKILL.md. A green test table is not",
    "evidence the host enforces anything."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/check-careful.sh\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "careful: checking for a destructive command"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/check-careful.sh\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "careful: checking for an edit to a guardrail file"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
